{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/86593-kueijin-laibon-mummy-hsien-shih-sorcerer-hunter-fallen-ect","id":86593,"title":"Kueijin, Laibon, Mummy, Hsien, Shih, Sorcerer, Hunter, Fallen ect?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-08T01:48:00-08:00","id":86593,"title":"Kueijin, Laibon, Mummy, Hsien, Shih, Sorcerer, Hunter, Fallen ect?","content":"So are there going to be updates on these gamelines? Are we going to get new information that we badly need if sales keep on rocking in Kickstarter? Have there been any news I missing? Since Darkage is coming around, I hoping for updates on DA specifics like Inquisition and Fae. But I've heard no updates on the Kindred of the East front for instance? We get awesome Hengeyokai Goodness at least! I think most of all I would reaaally want more on Mummy and Fallen! Fallen needs some updates and expansions on things like high level Demons, and interaction with the rest of the World, and Mummy just needs more love Period! We need a sequel to the Players guide to give high level love to the other mummies!<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh and more on Shih! Love Dem monks, and the Strike Force Zero they road in on!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","user":"Eldagusto","date":".  SHIH 03-08-2014, 04:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T08:34:53-08:00","id":86780,"title":"","content":"Demon Hunter X is my favorite segment of the Eastern story lines...Shih are so freaking cool!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2467-iris","name":"Iris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T14:36:25-08:00","id":87013,"title":"","content":"IIRC, Kindred of the East came out a year after Changeling did; so if the 20th Anniversary Edition fad extends that long, you should see it being considered in 2016. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d dearly love to see a line-neutral supplement featuring Numinous humans: e.g., sorcerers, psychics, and the faithful. I wouldn\u2019t stop at those three, either; I have ideas for at least two other kinds of Numina that would mesh with the themes and metaphysics of Werewolf and Mage; and I can see the former also meshing nicely with Wraith. <br /> <br /> Then there\u2019s the latter-days World of Darkness: Hunter, Mummy, Demon, and Orpheus. If these get commemorative editions, I don\u2019t want to wait until their 20th Anniversaries. They also have issues with being extremely metaplot-dependent. <br /> <br /> Mummy deserves special mention. It has never been a standalone game in the oWoD; even Mummy: the Resurrection required you to own another gameline\u2019s core book for the basic rules. As well, each of the three editions of Mummy was drastically different from the others. I <i>would</i> like a commemorative edition for Mummy; but given how drastically mummies changed with the coming of the ghost-storm, integrating both into a single game would prove tricky. And I\u2019m personally more fond of the pre-storm mummies than the post-storm ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T14:46:07-08:00","id":87016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/86593-kueijin-laibon-mummy-hsien-shih-sorcerer-hunter-fallen-ect?p=87013#post87013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, Kindred of the East came out a year after Changeling did; so if the 20th Anniversary Edition fad extends that long, you should see it being considered in 2016.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, KotE was 1998. You might have been knocked off-track by Dark Kingdom of Jade, which came out three years before the Year of the Lotus material did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T15:58:41-08:00","id":87055,"title":"","content":"We'll be seeing some Orpheus stuff in Wraith20. A full update might be a stretch goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T17:13:48-08:00","id":87095,"title":"","content":"Maybe the same way that they did one aggregated <i>Time of Judgment</i> book for many of the disparate and/or non-&quot;hardcover&quot; game lines, they'll do one special anniversary update for the referenced lines. In fact, I think that would be really sweet. WoD20","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T18:44:30-08:00","id":87140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_contai